01:08:26,458 --> 01:08:27,791
♪ <i>You can try, try, try </i>♪

980
01:08:27,875 --> 01:08:31,791
♪ <i>But you can't expect a demigod</i>
<i>To beat a decapod </i>♪

981
01:08:31,875 --> 01:08:32,958
♪ <i>Look it up </i>♪

982
01:08:33,041 --> 01:08:34,583
♪ <i>You will die, die, die </i>♪

983
01:08:34,666 --> 01:08:37,166
♪ <i>Now it's time for me to take apart </i>♪

984
01:08:37,250 --> 01:08:38,916
♪ <i>Your aching heart </i>♪

985
01:08:39,000 --> 01:08:43,958
♪ <i>Far from the ones who abandoned you </i>♪

986
01:08:44,041 --> 01:08:48,583
♪ <i>Chasing the love of these humans </i>♪

987
01:08:48,666 --> 01:08:51,958
♪ <i>Who made you feel wanted </i>♪

988
01:08:52,041 --> 01:08:54,750
♪ <i>You tried to be tough </i>♪

989
01:08:54,833 --> 01:08:58,708
♪ <i>But your armor's</i>
<i>Just not hard enough </i>♪

990
01:08:58,791 --> 01:09:03,416
♪ <i>Maui, and now it's time</i>
<i>To kick your heinie </i>♪

991
01:09:03,500 --> 01:09:06,500
♪ <i>Ever seen someone so shiny... </i>♪

992
01:09:06,583 --> 01:09:09,500
♪ <i>Soak it in cuz it's the last</i>
<i>You'll ever see </i>♪

993
01:09:09,583 --> 01:09:12,833
♪ <i>C'est la vie, mon ami</i>
<i>I'm so shiny </i>♪

994
01:09:12,916 --> 01:09:16,375
♪ <i>Now I eat you</i>
<i>So prepare your final plea </i>♪

995
01:09:16,458 --> 01:09:18,333
♪ <i>Just for me </i>♪

996
01:09:18,416 --> 01:09:21,541
♪ <i>You'll never be quite as shiny </i>♪

997
01:09:21,625 --> 01:09:26,500
♪ <i>You wish you were nice 'n' shiny </i>♪

998
01:09:28,208 --> 01:09:29,791
- Hey!
- Huh?

999
01:09:31,708 --> 01:09:33,375
I got something shiny for ya.

1000
01:09:33,458 --> 01:09:35,333
The heart of Te Fiti.

1001
01:09:35,416 --> 01:09:36,458
Don't give it to him, kid.

1002
01:09:36,541 --> 01:09:39,416
You want it? Come and get it.

1003
01:09:39,500 --> 01:09:41,750
You can't run from me.

1004
01:09:42,666 --> 01:09:45,250
Oh, you can. You keep surprising me.

1005
01:09:47,916 --> 01:09:51,625
There's only so far you can
get on those two little legs.

1006
01:09:51,708 --> 01:09:52,916
- You tripped.

1007
01:09:53,000 --> 01:09:55,708
Bad luck. -

1008
01:09:55,791 --> 01:09:59,958
Oh, the power of creation
for a crustacean.

1009
01:10:00,041 --> 01:10:04,125
Oh. Where is it? Where is it?

1010
01:10:04,208 --> 01:10:05,291
-

1011
01:10:05,375 --> 01:10:07,166
Come on, Te Fiti.

1012
01:10:07,666 --> 01:10:09,458
Time to go. Shall we?

1013
01:10:10,333 --> 01:10:12,208
- What about the heart?
- He can have it.

1014
01:10:12,291 --> 01:10:13,750
I've got a better one.

1015
01:10:13,833 --> 01:10:16,708
Yes! It is mine! It's...

1016
01:10:16,791 --> 01:10:17,833
Wait a minute.

1017
01:10:17,916 --> 01:10:19,583
I see, she's taken a barnacle

1018
01:10:19,666 --> 01:10:22,458
and she's covered it
in bioluminescent algae

1019
01:10:22,541 --> 01:10:23,666
as a diversion.

1020
01:10:25,208 --> 01:10:27,250
- Come back here!
- Over there!

1021
01:10:28,333 --> 01:10:30,416
There is no escape.

1022
01:10:30,500 --> 01:10:33,625
- And jump!
- Chee Hoo!

1023
01:10:33,708 --> 01:10:35,458
Oh, there is one escape.

1024
01:10:35,541 --> 01:10:37,166
Hey, did you like the song?

1025
01:10:37,250 --> 01:10:39,541
Did you have any notes or feedback?

1026
01:10:42,583 --> 01:10:44,208
-

1027
01:10:49,583 --> 01:10:52,250
Maui. Maui.

1028
01:10:55,416 --> 01:10:56,458
Ma--

1029
01:10:57,083 --> 01:11:00,708
Listen, I, uh, really appreciate
what you did down there.

1030
01:11:00,791 --> 01:11:02,583
That took guts. And I...

1031
01:11:03,458 --> 01:11:05,291
Oh. I get it.

1032
01:11:05,375 --> 01:11:07,666
Big, tough, handsome guy gets emotional.

1033
01:11:07,750 --> 01:11:10,625
And what do you do? You laugh in his face.

1034
01:11:10,708 --> 01:11:13,208
It's just you... you got this like...

1035
01:11:13,291 --> 01:11:15,291
Oh, no. Is there something on my face?

1036
01:11:15,791 --> 01:11:18,458
In my teeth? Is there
something in my teeth?

1037
01:11:18,541 --> 01:11:21,250
No, no. No, no, no. Shark head.

1038
01:11:21,333 --> 01:11:24,166
I-I like this part. I mean...
I mean the nice part.

1039
01:11:24,250 --> 01:11:27,583
I-I was not making fun
of the shark portion.

1040
01:11:27,666 --> 01:11:31,125
Look, the point is you did me a solid.

1041
01:11:31,208 --> 01:11:33,125
But you almost died.

1042
01:11:33,208 --> 01:11:35,208
And I couldn't even beat the dumb crab.

1043
01:11:35,291 --> 01:11:38,541
So, chances of beating Te Kā
are bubkes.

1044
01:11:38,625 --> 01:11:42,291
This mission has no chance
because you're still you

1045
01:11:42,375 --> 01:11:43,791
and I have a shark head.

1046
01:11:46,166 --> 01:11:48,958
♪ <i>Hey, it's okay, it's okay </i>♪

1047
01:11:49,041 --> 01:11:50,750
♪ <i>There's no wind </i>♪

1048
01:11:51,458 --> 01:11:55,916
♪ <i>We're dead soon</i>
<i>We're dead soon </i>♪

1049
01:11:56,000 --> 01:12:00,291
♪ <i>'Cause we're both gonna die</i>
<i>On this boat, hey </i>♪

1050
01:12:00,375 --> 01:12:02,500
Maybe try it with a smile.

1051
01:12:03,041 --> 01:12:04,458
Giant hawk.

1052
01:12:05,000 --> 01:12:08,541
-

1053
01:12:10,083 --> 01:12:14,541
♪ <i>Maui's gonna do</i>
<i>The dead man's float, hey </i>♪

1054
01:12:14,625 --> 01:12:15,958
Why are you being like this?

1055
01:12:16,041 --> 01:12:18,125
Leave me alone.

1056
01:12:22,291 --> 01:12:23,750
Both of you, leave me alone.

1057
01:12:27,458 --> 01:12:30,583
How do you get your tattoos?

1058
01:12:30,666 --> 01:12:34,000
They just show up... when I earn 'em.

1059
01:12:34,875 --> 01:12:35,875
They just show up.

1060
01:12:36,416 --> 01:12:38,500
How did you get that one?

1061
01:12:40,916 --> 01:12:42,875
That one's man's discovery of Nunya.

1062
01:12:42,958 --> 01:12:44,291
- What's Nunya?
- Nunya business.

1063
01:12:44,375 --> 01:12:46,666
- I'm just gonna keep asking.
- Drop it.

1064
01:12:46,750 --> 01:12:47,750
Why was that crab poking at it?

1065
01:12:47,833 --> 01:12:48,833
- Back off.
- What is it?

1066
01:12:48,916 --> 01:12:50,000
- No.
- What is it?

1067
01:12:50,083 --> 01:12:51,083
I don't want to talk about it.

1068
01:12:51,166 --> 01:12:52,125
Give it back!

1069
01:13:06,083 --> 01:13:08,833
If you don't want to talk, that's fine.

1070
01:13:10,541 --> 01:13:13,291
But my island, my people...

1071
01:13:15,250 --> 01:13:16,666
my family...

1072
01:13:19,375 --> 01:13:21,333
they won't survive if we don't make it.

1073
01:13:23,125 --> 01:13:24,500
I want to help.

1074
01:13:25,833 --> 01:13:27,166
If you let me.

1075
01:13:40,958 --> 01:13:42,708
I wasn't born a demigod.

1076
01:13:47,041 --> 01:13:48,625
I had human parents.

1077
01:13:50,291 --> 01:13:51,666
Who decided they didn't want me.

1078
01:13:54,708 --> 01:13:57,666
So they threw me in the ocean,
like I was nothing.

1079
01:13:58,541 --> 01:14:00,541
Somehow, I washed ashore.

1080
01:14:01,833 --> 01:14:03,125
Found by the gods.

1081
01:14:04,708 --> 01:14:06,041
They gave me my hook.

1082
01:14:07,166 --> 01:14:08,708
They made me Maui.

1083
01:14:09,875 --> 01:14:12,250
So back to the humans I went.

1084
01:14:13,291 --> 01:14:14,833
I gave them everything.

1085
01:14:15,833 --> 01:14:17,041
Islands,

1086
01:14:18,625 --> 01:14:19,875
fire,

1087
01:14:21,583 --> 01:14:22,791
coconuts.

1088
01:14:25,333 --> 01:14:27,458
I gave them anything they ever wanted.

1089
01:14:29,166 --> 01:14:31,625
You took the heart for us.

1090
01:14:33,791 --> 01:14:35,875
You did everything for us.

1091
01:14:37,375 --> 01:14:38,541
So we'd love you.

1092
01:14:41,458 --> 01:14:42,458
Yes.

1093
01:14:45,833 --> 01:14:46,916
It was never enough.

1094
01:14:47,000 --> 01:14:50,083
The ocean chose you too.

1095
01:14:50,166 --> 01:14:51,625
That's your takeaway?

1096
01:14:51,708 --> 01:14:55,333
Because it saw someone
worthy of being saved.

1097
01:14:55,416 --> 01:14:56,666
And what am I now?

1098
01:14:56,750 --> 01:14:57,958
You're Maui.

1099
01:14:59,416 --> 01:15:01,500
The gods didn't make that true.

1100
01:15:02,875 --> 01:15:04,083
You did.

1101
01:15:06,625 --> 01:15:08,333
Okay.

1102
01:15:09,416 --> 01:15:10,375
Okay.

1103
01:15:10,458 --> 01:15:12,000
Not in front of the guest.

1104
01:15:22,291 --> 01:15:23,291
The wind.

1105
01:15:24,083 --> 01:15:25,541
Maui, it's back.

1106
01:15:46,625 --> 01:15:47,833
Sorry, chicken.

1107
01:16:12,208 --> 01:16:14,250
-

1108
01:16:30,916 --> 01:16:31,958
Chee Hoo.

1109
01:17:00,166 --> 01:17:02,375
-

1110
01:18:11,208 --> 01:18:12,958
I figured it out.

1111
01:18:17,125 --> 01:18:20,083
You know, the ocean would love
when I would pull up the islands.

1112
01:18:20,166 --> 01:18:22,833
Your ancestors would voyage
her seas and find them.

1113
01:18:24,000 --> 01:18:27,083
That necklace you're wearing,
that belonged to Tautaivasa,

1114
01:18:27,166 --> 01:18:28,791
the first master wayfinder.

1115
01:18:29,458 --> 01:18:31,666
He knew no two voyages were the same.

1116
01:18:31,750 --> 01:18:32,833
Different every time.

1117
01:18:34,500 --> 01:18:35,875
A true wayfinder...

1118
01:18:37,208 --> 01:18:41,666
will see all the water... as a bridge...

1119
01:18:43,708 --> 01:18:44,708
and not a barrier.

1120
01:18:46,583 --> 01:18:48,333
And if I were the ocean,

1121
01:18:49,916 --> 01:18:53,125
I couldn't find a better curly-haired,

1122
01:18:53,208 --> 01:18:55,958
sidekick-having non-princess...

1123
01:18:59,541 --> 01:19:00,916
...to start voyaging again.

1124
01:19:01,625 --> 01:19:05,458
That is the nicest thing
you've ever said to me.

1125
01:19:05,541 --> 01:19:07,416
Probably should've saved it for Te Fiti.

1126
01:19:08,083 --> 01:19:09,083
I did.

1127
01:19:23,458 --> 01:19:25,666
- Moana, if I don't--
- You can do this.

1128
01:19:26,166 --> 01:19:27,166
You're Maui.

1129
01:19:30,541 --> 01:19:31,541
That's true.

1130
01:19:49,625 --> 01:19:51,291
It's Maui time.

1131
01:19:52,041 --> 01:19:53,541
Go save the world.

1132
01:19:55,708 --> 01:19:57,166
Chee Hoo!

1133
01:20:17,625 --> 01:20:18,833
Maui!

1134
01:20:40,666 --> 01:20:41,666
Maui.

1135
01:20:47,083 --> 01:20:49,291
We need to pull back. Now!

1136
01:20:54,083 --> 01:20:56,541
- What are you doing?
- Finding you a way in.

1137
01:20:57,125 --> 01:20:58,541
Now's our chance.

1138
01:20:59,583 --> 01:21:00,833
- Turn around.
- No.

1139
01:21:00,916 --> 01:21:02,583
- We're not gonna make it.
- Yes, we will.

1140
01:21:02,666 --> 01:21:04,875
- Moana, stop!
- No! I can do it.

1141
01:21:37,250 --> 01:21:38,416
Are you okay?

1142
01:21:39,583 --> 01:21:40,541
Maui?

1143
01:21:40,625 --> 01:21:41,916
I told you to turn back.

1144
01:21:43,125 --> 01:21:44,916
- I thought we could make it.
- "We"?

1145
01:21:50,916 --> 01:21:52,333
I thought I could make it.

1146
01:22:08,541 --> 01:22:09,916
I'll find a way to fix your hook.

1147
01:22:10,000 --> 01:22:11,916
The gods made my hook.

1148
01:22:12,416 --> 01:22:14,000
You can't fix it.

1149
01:22:14,625 --> 01:22:16,125
Next time I'll be more careful.

1150
01:22:16,208 --> 01:22:18,041
- There's no next time.
- But now we know

1151
01:22:18,125 --> 01:22:19,791
Te Kā can't follow us
into the water.

1152
01:22:19,875 --> 01:22:21,375
We can find another way around.

1153
01:22:21,458 --> 01:22:24,041
There is no other way. I'm not going back.

1154
01:22:24,125 --> 01:22:26,708
Take a look at my hook.
One more hit and it's over.

1155
01:22:26,791 --> 01:22:28,958
But my people, my island...

1156
01:22:29,041 --> 01:22:31,500
Without my hook,

1157
01:22:32,375 --> 01:22:33,875
I am nothing.

1158
01:22:33,958 --> 01:22:37,291
We're only here 'cause you stole the heart
in the first place.

1159
01:22:37,375 --> 01:22:38,375
No.

1160
01:22:39,041 --> 01:22:40,333
We're here

1161
01:22:40,416 --> 01:22:43,666
because the ocean told you
that you were special.

1162
01:22:45,250 --> 01:22:46,333
And you believed it.

1163
01:22:48,083 --> 01:22:50,250
- I am Moana of Motunui.
- Goodbye, Moana.

1164
01:22:50,333 --> 01:22:52,000
You will sail across the sea
and restore the heart...

1165
01:22:52,083 --> 01:22:54,458
I'm not killing myself so you can prove
you're something you're not.

1166
01:22:54,541 --> 01:22:57,708
The ocean chose me! It chose us!

1167
01:22:58,958 --> 01:23:00,166
It chose wrong.

1168
01:23:01,375 --> 01:23:03,000
- Goodbye, Moana.
- Maui!

1169
01:23:03,541 --> 01:23:05,458
-

1170
01:23:13,041 --> 01:23:15,416
Maui, no! Don't go!

1171
01:23:24,375 --> 01:23:25,291
Maui?

1172
01:23:37,833 --> 01:23:40,041
Ocean, why did you bring me here?

1173
01:23:42,916 --> 01:23:44,750
I was never the right person.

1174
01:23:50,541 --> 01:23:52,500
You should choose someone else.

1175
01:23:54,958 --> 01:23:56,291
Please.

1176
01:23:58,083 --> 01:23:59,083
Please.

1177
01:25:21,208 --> 01:25:24,125
You're a long ways past the reef.

1178
01:25:28,083 --> 01:25:29,375
Gramma.

1179
01:25:29,458 --> 01:25:32,708
I guess I chose the right tattoo.

1180
01:25:46,708 --> 01:25:48,791
I tried, Gramma, but...

1181
01:25:49,416 --> 01:25:50,916
I couldn't do it.

1182
01:25:52,125 --> 01:25:53,416
I can't do it.

1183
01:25:54,708 --> 01:25:56,875
If you're ready to go home,

1184
01:25:56,958 --> 01:25:59,000
I will be with you.

1185
01:26:15,666 --> 01:26:18,000
Why do you hesitate?

1186
01:26:22,958 --> 01:26:24,166
I don't know.

1187
01:26:25,458 --> 01:26:28,500
♪ <i>I know a girl from an island </i>♪

1188
01:26:29,041 --> 01:26:31,708
♪ <i>She stands apart from the crowd </i>♪

1189
01:26:32,500 --> 01:26:35,125
♪ <i>She loves the sea and her people </i>♪

1190
01:26:36,166 --> 01:26:38,833
♪ <i>She makes her whole family proud </i>♪

1191
01:26:39,583 --> 01:26:42,583
♪ <i>Sometimes the world seems against you </i>♪

1192
01:26:43,208 --> 01:26:45,958
♪ <i>The journey may leave a scar </i>♪

1193
01:26:46,708 --> 01:26:49,083
♪ <i>But scars can heal and reveal </i>♪

1194
01:26:49,166 --> 01:26:52,083
♪ <i>Just where you are... </i>♪

1195
01:26:53,875 --> 01:26:56,291
♪ <i>The people you love will change you </i>♪

1196
01:26:56,875 --> 01:26:59,500
♪ <i>The things you have learned</i>
<i>Will guide you </i>♪

1197
01:27:00,416 --> 01:27:03,083
♪ <i>And nothing on earth can silence </i>♪

1198
01:27:03,625 --> 01:27:06,833
♪ <i>The quiet voice still inside you </i>♪

1199
01:27:06,916 --> 01:27:10,041
♪ <i>And when that voice starts to whisper </i>♪

1200
01:27:10,583 --> 01:27:13,583
♪ <i>"Moana, you've come so far" </i>♪

1201
01:27:14,583 --> 01:27:16,000
♪ <i>Moana, listen... </i>♪

1202
01:27:16,625 --> 01:27:21,250
♪ <i>Do you know who you are? </i>♪

1203
01:27:24,250 --> 01:27:25,375
Who am I?

1204
01:27:28,250 --> 01:27:31,541
♪ <i>I am a girl who loves my island </i>♪

1205
01:27:31,625 --> 01:27:34,583
♪ <i>And the girl who loves the sea </i>♪

1206
01:27:36,125 --> 01:27:39,500
♪ <i>It calls me </i>♪

1207
01:27:41,333 --> 01:27:44,375
♪ <i>I am the daughter of the village chief </i>♪

1208
01:27:44,458 --> 01:27:47,583
♪ <i>We are descended from voyagers </i>♪

1209
01:27:47,666 --> 01:27:50,666
♪ <i>Who found their way across the world </i>♪

1210
01:27:50,750 --> 01:27:53,250
♪ <i>They call me </i>♪

1211
01:27:54,375 --> 01:27:56,541
♪ <i>I've delivered us to where we are </i>♪

1212
01:27:57,250 --> 01:27:59,583
♪ <i>I have journeyed farther </i>♪

1213
01:28:00,541 --> 01:28:02,875
♪ <i>I am everything I've learned and more </i>♪

1214
01:28:02,958 --> 01:28:06,583
♪ <i>Still it calls me </i>♪

1215
01:28:07,125 --> 01:28:09,250
♪ <i>And the call isn't out there at all </i>♪

1216
01:28:09,333 --> 01:28:12,250
♪ <i>It's inside me </i>♪

1217
01:28:12,333 --> 01:28:14,250
♪ <i>It's like the tide </i>♪

1218
01:28:14,333 --> 01:28:18,875
♪ <i>Always falling and rising </i>♪

1219
01:28:18,958 --> 01:28:21,500
♪ <i>I will carry you here in my heart </i>♪

1220
01:28:21,583 --> 01:28:24,541
♪ <i>You remind me </i>♪

1221
01:28:24,625 --> 01:28:27,208
♪ <i>That come what may </i>♪

1222
01:28:27,291 --> 01:28:30,250
♪ <i>I know the way </i>♪

1223
01:28:30,333 --> 01:28:34,875
♪ <i>I am Moana! </i>♪

1224
01:29:02,500 --> 01:29:04,541
<i>I am Moana of Motunui.</i>

